# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ — never commit any of it.
#
# The exports carry the account holder's full name, service address and account
# numbers, plus a year of 15-minute electricity readings, which is enough to
# reconstruct sleep schedules and identify the weeks the house was empty. The
# PDF bills carry the same identifiers in plainer form.
#
# The whole directory is ignored rather than a list of filenames, so a new
# export cannot be committed by accident merely because nobody remembered to
# add its name here.
#
# data/noaa/ goes with it. That is public NOAA data with no PII, but it is also
# regenerable in one command, so there is nothing to gain from an exception
# that would weaken the rule:
#     python3 tools/fetch_noaa.py
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/

# The generated dashboard embeds the same usage data. Keep it local.
build/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# WSL download markers
*:Zone.Identifier
